  "id": "tax.us.2025.rule.form1040-line12e",
  "notes": "Core v67 (gambling-losses) successor: Schedule A line 16 (gambling losses limited to winnings) joins the itemized side on every route. With a Form 1098 statement the itemized figure is line 8a plus line 16. With no statement it is the hand-entered itemized total plus line 16; when the hand-entered total and line 16 are both nonzero the rule blocks by name (ITEMIZED_TOTAL_WITH_GAMBLING_LOSSES) so losses cannot be counted twice (the block's own code is not in the closed blocked-code set, so the row reads DEPENDENCY_INVALID on this rule and this note is the reason), and a filer with no hand-entered total itemizes on line 16 alone when it exceeds the standard deduction. Successor adds the derived Schedule A total as an explicit completion dependency. Existing empty, no-statement, and line8a selection behavior is otherwise unchanged; a blocked connected line8a cannot be bypassed through raw itemized deductions.",
